  "notes": "{構成|こうせい} means \"composition\" or \"structure\"—how parts are arranged to form a whole. Can be used as a noun or する verb.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜で{構成|こうせい}される: to be composed of ~\n- 〜を{構成|こうせい}する: to compose, to make up\n- {構成|こうせい}を{考|かんが}える: to think about the structure\n\nCOMMON COMPOUNDS:\n- {構成|こうせい}{要素|ようそ}: component, element\n- {構成|こうせい}{員|いん}: member, constituent\n- {家族|かぞく}{構成|こうせい}: family composition\n- {文|ぶん}の{構成|こうせい}: sentence structure\n\nUSAGE CONTEXTS: Used in writing, organization, design, and analysis—anywhere parts combine to form a whole.",
